{"id":15546,"artist":"Les Miserables.  Kar","title":"A Little Fall of Rain","lyrics_plain":"(Eponine)\nDon't you fret, M'sieur Marius\nI don't feel any pain\nA little fall of rain\nCan hardly hurt me now\nYou're here, that's all I need to know\nAnd you will keep me safe\nAnd you will keep me close\nAnd rain will make the flowers grow.\n(Marius)\nBut you will live,\n'Ponine, dear God above,\nIf I could heal your wounds with words of love.\n(Eponine)\nJust hold me now, and let it be.\nShelter me, comfort me\n(Marius)\nYou would live a hundred years\nIf I could show you how\nI won't desert you now\n(Eponine)\nThe rain can't hurt me now\nThis rain will wash away what's past\nAnd you will keep me safe\nAnd you will keep me close\nI'll sleep in your embrace at last.\nThe rain that brings you here\nIs Heaven blessed!\nThe skies begin to clear\nAnd I'm at rest\nA breath away from where you are\nI've come home from so far\n(Both)\nHushabye, dear Eponine,\nYou (I)  won't feel any pain\nA little fall of rain\nCan hardly hurt me (you) now\n(Marius)\nI'm here\n(Eponine)\nThat's all I need to know\n(Both)\nAnd you (I)  will keep(stay) me safe\nAnd you will keep me close\n(Eponine) And rain\n(Marius) And rain\n(Both)\nWill make the flowers . . grow.","lyrics_synced":"[00:03.69] (Eponine)\n[00:07.62] Don't you fret, M'sieur Marius\n[00:10.85] I don't feel any pain\n[00:14.54] A little fall of rain\n[00:18.00] Can hardly hurt me now\n[00:21.69] You're here, that's all I need to know\n[00:27.23] And you will keep me safe\n[00:30.92] And you will keep me close\n[00:34.62] And rain will make the flowers grow.\n[00:40.62] (Marius)\n[00:41.31] But you will live,\n[00:43.15] 'Ponine, dear God above,\n[00:48.46] If I could heal your wounds with words of love.\n[00:53.54] (Eponine)\n[00:54.00] Just hold me now, and let it be.\n[00:58.15] Shelter me, comfort me\n[01:02.77] (Marius)\n[01:03.69] You would live a hundred years\n[01:07.15] If I could show you how\n[01:10.85] I won't desert you n